ved_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-09T17:07:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T08:45:48Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4 beta3, 4.3 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows\n\n### Issue description\n\nCame up while investigating something else. Reimporting the image causes the rendering server path (the one returned from `RenderingServer.get_texture_path()` to be lost. The cause seems to be that reloading the texture resource calls `RenderingServer.texture_replace()`, which invalidates the path.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download the MRP\n2. Open the scene\n3. Press the tool button that calls `RenderingServer.get_texture_path(), it will print the path correctly\n4. Reimport icon.svg\n5. Press the tool button again, the path is lost\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_proj.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18725436/test_proj.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102622/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}